From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rdoupe
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 13:14:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 26/26] Keep the NVIDIA GPU asleep while apps start on hybrids

The open NVIDIA driver resumes a runtime-suspended GPU for every call
into it, even one that only asks which GPUs exist. On a hybrid laptop
whose iGPU drives the display, any app that lists Vulkan devices or
opens surfaceless or device EGL at startup (GTK, Chromium, Electron)
woke the dGPU for about 20 seconds, whichever GPU it went on to use. On
the Zephyrus G16 that was most of a day's unexplained wakes. A trace
there showed Vulkan enumeration with NVIDIA's ICD present and
surfaceless/device EGL in the stock vendor order waking it; Radeon's ICD
alone, or Mesa first for surfaceless EGL, kept it asleep. Radeon first
with NVIDIA still listed woke it too, and GLVND asks every listed EGL
vendor for its devices whatever their order.

VK_LOADER_DRIVERS_DISABLE=*nvidia* and only Mesa's EGL vendor are now
set there, on Turing and newer, for the desktop: the shell, the
launcher, key bindings and the apps they start. Never for Hyprland
itself, since aquamarine opens EGL on the dGPU for a monitor on its
ports (HDMI on the G16): the new desktop-gpu-pins.lua, loaded before any
binding or rule is made, wraps hl.exec_cmd, hl.dsp.exec_cmd,
hl.dsp.exec_raw and hl.workspace_rule's on_created_empty, so each
command Hyprland runs exports the pins in its own shell first, after
any exec rules. Games get both back however they start:

- autostart.lua takes the pins back out of the systemd user environment
  after exporting the rest, so what systemd starts, a game launcher at
  login included, has every GPU;
- an interactive bash drops them (default/bash/envs), so anything run
  from a terminal does too;
- the app launcher starts game entries through the new
  omarchy-launch-desktop-entry without them: the Game category,
  PrefersNonDefaultGPU or X-KDE-RunOnDiscreteGpu, or an Exec that runs
  steam, lutris, heroic, bottles, umu-run, gamescope, wine or proton
  (desktop IDs of entries in subdirectories resolved as gtk-launch
  does); installing Steam starts it the same way;
- the new omarchy-launch-all-gpus runs anything else with every GPU.

OMARCHY_DESKTOP_GPU_PINS names the pins for bash, so a value of the
user's own is left alone. A migration asks for a reboot while the
session predates the pins, and another while Hyprland itself still
carries them (1.107 to 1.112 set them for Hyprland too, so an HDMI
monitor plugged in after login never appeared).

Fork commits c02f91e3, 8769c24c, 02c9d61f, 6ef8e273, e71057d9 and
f1a38066 on asus/v4-5-0-rc1, squashed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
